Looking at this problem, I need to divide n distinct integers into two sets A and B with specific constraints:
- If x ∈ A, then (a-x) must also be in A
- If x ∈ B, then (b-x) must also be in B

The key insight is that elements can be grouped into connected components based on whether their complements exist in the input. Within each component, all elements must go to the same set (all A or all B). For a component to be valid, either:
1. All elements have their A-complements also present in the component (can all go to A)
2. All elements have their B-complements also present in the component (can all go to B)

If neither is possible for any component, output NO, otherwise output YES with the assignment.

```python
def solution(input_str):
    lines = input_str.strip().split('\n')
    n, a, b = map(int, lines[0].split())
    p = list(map(int, lines[1].split()))

    number_to_index = {x: i for i, x in enumerate(p)}
    parent = list(range(n))

    def find(x):
        if parent[x] != x:
            parent[x] = find(parent[x])
        return parent[x]

    def union(x, y):
        px, py = find(x), find(y)
        if px != py:
            parent[px] = py

    # Union A pairs (elements that must be together if in set A)
    for i in range(n):
        complement_a = a - p[i]
        if complement_a in number_to_index:
            idx_comp_a = number_to_index[complement_a]
            union(i, idx_comp_a)

    # Union B pairs (elements that must be together if in set B)
    for i in range(n):
        complement_b = b - p[i]
        if complement_b in number_to_index:
            idx_comp_b = number_to_index[complement_b]
            union(i, idx_comp_b)

    # For each component, check if it can be assigned to A or B
    comp_valid_a = {}
    comp_valid_b = {}

    for i in range(n):
        root = find(i)
        if root not in comp_valid_a:
            # Check if all elements in this component can go to set A
            comp_valid_a[root] = True
            for j in range(n):
                if find(j) == root:
                    complement_a = a - p[j]
                    if complement_a not in p:
                        comp_valid_a[root] = False
                        break

            # Check if all elements in this component can go to set B
            comp_valid_b[root] = True
            for j in range(n):
                if find(j) == root:
                    complement_b = b - p[j]
                    if complement_b not in p:
                        comp_valid_b[root] = False
                        break

    assignment = [0] * n
    for i in range(n):
        root = find(i)
        if not comp_valid_a[root] and not comp_valid_b[root]:
            return "NO\n"

        # If can go to B, assign to B (1), otherwise to A (0)
        if comp_valid_b[root]:
            assignment[i] = 1
        else:
            assignment[i] = 0

    return "YES\n" + " ".join(map(str, assignment)) + " \n"

